      },
      "worked": "A valid integer base satisfies $a\\ge2$. Let $k=\\log_a(256)$ be an integer. Since $a>1$ and $256>1$, $k$ is positive.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a^k&=256\\\\a^k&=2^8\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe only prime factor of $a$ can be 2, so write $a=2^m$, where $m$ is a positive integer.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2^{mk}&=2^8\\\\mk&=8\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $m$ is a positive divisor of 8: $m=1,2,4,8$. Hence $a=2,4,16,256$. These give logarithms $8,4,2,1$, respectively.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
